---
/**
 * Records the campaign touch for this page load. Renders nothing.
 *
 * It has to be on every page, not only the ones with a form: the case it
 * exists for is a visitor who arrives on an ad, reads three pages, and then
 * submits from a fourth. By then `location.search` is empty. Without this,
 * that lead reaches Google Ads with no click id and is attributed to nothing.
 *
 * `src/lib/attribution.ts` holds the rules — first touch is never overwritten,
 * only a campaign arrival updates the last touch, and direct or internal
 * navigation updates neither. It also holds the retention decision: session
 * scope by default, because a 90-day marketing identifier store is a consent
 * question this site has not answered.
 */
---

<script>
  import { recordTouch } from '../lib/attribution';

  /* Wrapped because it must never be able to break a page. Private browsing
     throws on the first storage access, and an attribution record is not
     worth a blank screen. */
  try {
    recordTouch();
  } catch {
    /* no attribution for this visit; the page is unaffected */
  }
</script>
